Package: engine1999
Architecture: any
Section: devel
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
         binutils,
         libc6-dev | libc-dev,
         libsdl2-dev,
Suggests: engine1999-games, engine1999-doc
Description: 2D game engine simulating a 1980s home computer, with a BASIC
 Engine1999 behaves like a home computer of the late 1980s and early 1990s:
 an 80x25 text screen, tile, graphics and sprite layers, a software
 synthesizer, files and devices, and a built-in BASIC dialect with
 procedures, timers, sprite paths, a UI toolkit and editors for sprites,
 music and sound effects.
 .
 The BUILD statement turns a program into a standalone executable using
 the system linker; for that this package depends on binutils, the C
 library and SDL2 development files. It contains the window version
 (engine1999), the console version without a window (engine1999c), the
 BUILD kit and the demo programs.

Package: engine1999-games
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: demo games written in Engine1999 BASIC
 Fruit Invaders (I to III), The Long Climb (I and II), Madrun (I and II),
 Eternal River (I and II), Being a Rustball, and Hunt the Wumpus (a text
 game for any terminal), each built into a program of its own
 (engine1999-<name>) with its own manual page. The sources are in the
 engine1999 package (/usr/share/engine1999/demos).

Package: engine1999-doc
Architecture: all
Section: doc
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: documentation of Engine1999
 The language reference, the grammar quick reference, the graphics, sound,
 I/O, UI, library and security documentation of Engine1999.
